#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:5
#: 18029b2a9e424c10a71fdd7c598d39da
msgid "Steering Input Type and Reversing Behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:7
#: 370eddd613c8497dbfc647cd38d7874d
msgid "The :ref:`PILOT_STEER_TYPE <PILOT_STEER_TYPE>` parameter provides control of two behaviours related to the pilot's steering input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:10
#: 5933f3c22923429a891e782d5040313b
msgid "Two Paddle Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:12
#: b6d5e99db1c44b40b621964c900f83d3
msgid "Normally the user (aka Pilot) controls the vehicle using one transmitter channel for steering (i.e. move a stick left-right) and another for throttle (move a stick forward-back) but it is also possible to control the steering and direction with two sticks (both moving forward-back) as if controlling two wheels of a skid-steer vehicle (like R2D2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:14
#: d8166e92d8ae4124a2cc687e8fed3d98
msgid "This Two Paddle Input method can be enabled by setting :ref:`PILOT_STEER_TYPE <PILOT_STEER_TYPE>` to \"1\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:16
#: b688ae8501594fa9a1e9fc56a08bd68b
msgid "Once enabled, raising RC input 1 channel high is like controlling the left motor of a skid-steer vehicle so the vehicle will turn right.  Raising RC input channel 3 is like controlling the right motor so the vehicle will turn left.  Raising both channels high will cause the vehicle to move forward, lowering both will cause the vehicle to backup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:20
#: 8fb0732f24324f168f3abd2ccf977336
msgid "Most users of skid steering vehicles should leave the :ref:`PILOT_STEER_TYPE <PILOT_STEER_TYPE>` parameter at the default of \"0\" meaning the pilot controls the vehicle using one RC input for throttle and another for steering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:23
#: d97af2e05ba04f6b8e9269e19ddeefb3
msgid "Reversing Behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:25
#: a51705cbf92344288412983ad84bd663
msgid "ArduPilot Rover's reversing behaviour is just like a full sized car, regardless of whether the vehicle is a regular steering-throttle style vehicle or a skid-steering vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:27
#: 1b26327eaaad4da798d94fbb44710f0c
msgid "if moving forward with wheel turned right, vehicle turns in clockwise direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:28
#: fce3ce98202c4b2ba42084a2d35204f0
msgid "if moving backwards with wheel turned right, vehicles turns in counter-clockwise direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-steering-input-type-and-reversing-behaviour.rst:30
#: 983f0d1b0e764440b02603163d9c14fe
msgid "Some users, especially users of skid-steering vehicles and omni vehicles, may wish the vehicle's turning direction to be the same whether moving forward or reversing.  This can be accomplished by setting :ref:`PILOT_STEER_TYPE <PILOT_STEER_TYPE>` to \"3\""
msgstr ""
